    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0693" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg651"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 17, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 13th instant, transmitting a copy of a despatch from
                    the governor of the Bahama islands, stating that, with reference to the reported
                    fitting out of a vessel at Nassau, N. P., to cruise against the shipping of the
                    United States, the result <pb facs="0694" n="652" xml:id="pg652"/> of inquiries
                    which he has made convinces him that no vessel is fitting out there for that
                    purpose, and to thank you for your prompt attention to the matter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
